Contract matches current API source. GET /auth/organization/deletion is the auth-handler endpoint at basePath /auth. A 200 body is { blocked, code, message } from OrganizationRetention.organizationDeletion. code is ERP_REFERENCE or null. There is no allowed field. blocked false only means organizationOccupancy returned no message; the handler still requires organization:delete before that body, and blocked false does not authorize deletion. POST /auth/organization/delete still runs beforeDeleteOrganization, which uses the same organizationOccupancy check and returns 409 ERP_REFERENCE. The preflight does not delete unused owners.

Web mismatch: apps/web does not call that GET. EditOrganizationForm shows Delete from the local organization:delete check, and organizationApi.remove only handles ERP_REFERENCE after authClient.organization.delete. WebApproved still owns that client change.
